// CROWN partiality (TRAP, 2026-10-06): a sequence read traps past its
// sequence, so a read whose bounds nothing here proves performs Trap, and a
// declared `!Trap` over it refuses. `xs` is a parameter, so no length is in
// sight. Checked clean on boot 4228ff71: the deliberate trap beneath every
// read (lib/memory's out_of_range) was rowed Memory alone. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
fn sixth(xs) with !Trap = xs[5]

fn main() = sixth([1, 2, 3])
